            "id": 1463,
            "sort": 1,
            "name": "Introduction",
            "value": "<p>In contemporary society, news media have become increasingly powerful in shaping public opinion and daily life. This phenomenon can be attributed to technological advances, and I believe it brings both benefits and drawbacks.</p>",
            "question_id": 17818,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1473,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p><strong>The enhanced influence of news media stems from two main factors.</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">Firstly, smartphones have made news consumption accessible everywhere, allowing people to read updates during their commute through instant notifications that alert users to breaking news. This means information reaches audiences immediately, significantly expanding media reach.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\">Additionally, people now spend considerably more time on digital devices, resulting in greater exposure to news content as social media feeds constantly display news updates, leading to higher consumption of information.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 17818,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1478,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<p><strong>Regarding whether this development is positive or negative, I believe it has mixed implications.</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">On the positive side, citizens become better informed about world events, as people learn about global issues and develop a better understanding of politics and society. This enables them to make informed decisions and improve their civic participation.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\"> </span>However, the negative aspect lies in how misinformation and fake news spread easily through these platforms. Unverified information spreads quickly, causing people to believe false stories, which creates confusion and wrong beliefs that can be harmful to society.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 17818,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1479,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Conclusion",
            "value": "<p>In conclusion, news media's increased influence results from smartphone accessibility and higher digital device usage. While this development helps create more informed citizens, it also poses risks through the rapid spread of misinformation.</p>",
